/*!
\page page_stistHitCollection StIstHitCollection — Collection Documentation

\ref StIstHitCollection is the top-level container for all reconstructed
Intermediate Silicon Tracker (IST) hits in a single STAR event.  The IST was
the middle layer of the STAR Heavy Flavour Tracker (HFT), bridging the PXL
pixel detector and the outer SSD/SST layer for track extrapolation in
heavy-flavour vertex finding.  Hits are organised in a three-level hierarchy:
detector → ladder → sensor.

\see StIstHitCollection
\see StIstLadderHitCollection
\see StIstSensorHitCollection
\see StIstHit

---

\section ist_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
StIstHitCollection                   (top-level, one per event)
└── StIstLadderHitCollection           [kIstNumLadders=24 ladders, indices 0–23]
    └── StIstSensorHitCollection         [kIstNumSensorsPerLadder=6 sensors, indices 0–5]
        └── StSPtrVecIstHit                (owns the StIstHit objects)
\endcode

The constants \c kIstNumLadders (24) and \c kIstNumSensorsPerLadder (6) are
defined in \c StEvent/StEnumerations.h inside the \c StIstConsts namespace.

All sub-collection nodes are embedded (stack-allocated) inside their parent;
no heap allocation is used for collection nodes.

\section ist_containment Containment Model

| Level    | Class                          | Contents                                    |
|----------|--------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Detector | \ref StIstHitCollection        | 24 \ref StIstLadderHitCollection objects    |
| Ladder   | \ref StIstLadderHitCollection  | 6 \ref StIstSensorHitCollection objects     |
| Sensor   | \ref StIstSensorHitCollection  | `StSPtrVecIstHit` of `StIstHit*`            |

\section ist_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StIstSensorHitCollection holds its hits in a member of type
\c StSPtrVecIstHit, which is a **smart-pointer vector** that **owns** the
\ref StIstHit objects it contains.  The \ref StIstSensorHitCollection destructor
explicitly deletes every hit in the vector (necessary because \ref StIstHit
provides its own pool-allocated \c new/delete).

Ladder and sensor sub-collections are embedded members of their parent classes
and are destroyed automatically with the parent.  \ref StIstHitCollection itself
is owned by the StEvent framework (\c St_DataSet / \c StXRefMain).

\warning Do **not** delete individual \ref StIstHit pointers obtained from the
collection.  The collection manages their lifetimes.

\section ist_members Data Members

\subsection ist_members_top StIstHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StIstLadderHitCollection[24]` | `mLadders` | Fixed-size array of 24 ladder sub-collections, sized by `kIstNumLadders`. |
| `UChar_t` | `mClusteringType` | Identifier for the clustering algorithm used to produce the hits. |

\subsection ist_members_ladder StIstLadderHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StIstSensorHitCollection[6]` | `mSensors` | Fixed-size array of 6 sensor sub-collections per ladder, sized by `kIstNumSensorsPerLadder`. |

\subsection ist_members_sensor StIstSensorHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StSPtrVecIstHit` | `mHits` | Smart-pointer vector of `StIstHit*`; owns all contained hits. |

\section ist_methods Key Methods

\subsection ist_methods_top StIstHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `addHit(StIstHit*)` | `bool` | Routes hit to correct ladder/sensor. Returns `false` if any index is out of range. |
| `numberOfHits() const` | `unsigned int` | Total hits across all ladders and sensors. |
| `getClusteringType() const` | `unsigned char` | Returns the clustering algorithm type identifier. |
| `setClusteringType(unsigned char)` | `void` | Sets the clustering algorithm type identifier. |
| `ladder(unsigned int)` | `StIstLadderHitCollection*` | 0-based ladder access; returns `nullptr` if out of range. |

\subsection ist_methods_ladder StIstLadderHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `numberOfHits() const` | `unsigned int` | Total hits on this ladder. |
| `sensor(unsigned int)` | `StIstSensorHitCollection*` | 0-based sensor access; returns `nullptr` if out of range. |

\subsection ist_methods_sensor StIstSensorHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `hits()` | `StSPtrVecIstHit&` | Mutable reference to the hit vector. |
| `hits() const` | `const StSPtrVecIstHit&` | Const reference to the hit vector. |

\section ist_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StIstHitCollection* istColl = event->istHitCollection();
if (!istColl) return;

for (unsigned int iLad = 0; iLad < kIstNumLadders; ++iLad) {
    const StIstLadderHitCollection* ladderColl = istColl->ladder(iLad);
    if (!ladderColl) continue;

    for (unsigned int iSen = 0; iSen < kIstNumSensorsPerLadder; ++iSen) {
        const StIstSensorHitCollection* senColl = ladderColl->sensor(iSen);
        if (!senColl) continue;

        const StSPtrVecIstHit& hits = senColl->hits();
        for (const StIstHit* hit : hits) {
            // process hit ...
        }
    }
}
\endcode
*/
